Well, when you get in the higher experience levels, your chance to hit
enemies with any weapon goes up pretty quick. Even at unskilled, a
higher level character shouldn't have a problem using one. When you're
hitting every time, then it's easy to raise it to basic->skilled etc.
As for lower levels, you can try to go up into the dungeon and fight
easier monsters - these will be easier to hit. Get your skill to basic
on the easy creatures and then move on from there.

I'm still a nethack newbie, but the only time i've really used polearms
is when:
- i'm fighting a water based enemy (eel, etc)
- i can't cast a spell like magic missiles or similar to kill it
- i don't have a wand i can use to kill it, or don't want to use it
- my "normal" ranged attack would lose a lot of items in the water and
i'm running low/conserving

that being said, ranged attack > no ranged attack.

